{"kind":"request","text":"Bound the whole-projection response the resident serves.","body":{"conditions":"Measured at main 316d5aeb (docs/reference/performance.md): the resident's full projection response is 11.2 MB at 5,786 records, about 1.94 KiB per record, and grows linearly because the linear-history projection retains every application event. At FIRST-PRODUCTION's 500,000 records that is about 970 MB, which cannot meet the 2 s warm-status target regardless of fold speed; warm latency itself is flat and healthy at 10-30 ms, so size rather than compute is the miss. gs status --json and --all are documented as uncapped. Suspected bounding component: unbounded full-projection serialization. Satisfied when a client can obtain current workroom state at 500,000 records within the 2 s target, without removing callers' ability to obtain the complete projection when they ask for it.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}